CAT = "sgrtSkills"; SEG = "SKL"
Q = [
("You switch on the ignition before starting the engine. How do you confirm the bike is not in gear?",
 "The green N light is on", ["The red oil light is on", "The tachometer reads zero", "The horn sounds"],
 "When the ignition is on, check visually that the green neutral lamp is lit before pressing the starter."),
("After starting the engine to move off from the kerb, what do you do first?",
 "Signal right", ["Signal left", "Open the throttle fully", "Let go of the front brake"],
 "Once the engine is running, signal right to show you intend to move off from the kerbside, then change your leg positions."),
("Moving off, which foot goes on the ground while you select first gear?",
 "Your right foot", ["Your left foot", "Both feet", "Neither; both stay on the pegs"],
 "Put your right foot down and your left foot on the footrest to select first. Then lower the left foot and put the right foot back on its rest."),
("What engine speed should you hold as you move off?",
 "2,000 to 3,000 rpm", ["500 to 1,000 rpm", "6,000 to 7,000 rpm", "The red zone"],
 "Open the throttle slightly to about 2,000 to 3,000 rpm. Too few revs and the engine may stall."),
("What happens at the clutch's biting point?",
 "The engine revs dip slightly", ["The engine cuts out", "The rear brake comes on", "The gear changes itself"],
 "As you ease the clutch out to the biting point, or half clutch, the engine revs drop a little because the drive is starting to take up."),
("What happens if you release the clutch lever suddenly when moving off?",
 "The engine stalls", ["The rear brake locks", "The gear jumps to neutral", "The headlight dims"],
 "Ease the clutch out to the biting point and then gradually. A sudden release stalls the engine; holding the half clutch too long wears the linings."),
("When stopping behind a stationary vehicle, how much space should you leave?",
 "One motorcycle length", ["Five metres exactly", "Almost touching its bumper", "About three car lengths"],
 "Stop about a motorcycle length behind the vehicle in front, so you have room to move around it."),
("You are pulling in to stop at the side of the road. Which check comes just before you move left?",
 "Look over your left shoulder", ["Look over your right shoulder", "Sound the horn twice", "Switch off the engine"],
 "Check the road ahead and your mirrors, signal left, look over your left shoulder for your blind spot, then move left and brake."),
("After stopping, you put the gearbox into neutral. How hard should you tap the gear pedal?",
 "Lightly", ["Firmly to the bottom", "Twice, quickly", "Not at all; use the clutch"],
 "Tap the gear pedal lightly to find neutral. Tapping too firmly may select first gear instead."),
("Which side should you dismount on?",
 "The left side", ["The right side", "Either side", "Over the handlebar"],
 "With the front brake applied, dismount to the left and set the main stand or side stand."),
("How do you lock the steering when you park?",
 "Bars fully left, key to LOCK", ["Bars fully right, key out", "Bars straight, key to OFF", "First gear, engine stopped"],
 "Turn the handlebar all the way to the left, push the key down and turn it to LOCK, then remove the key. This helps prevent theft."),
("How early should you signal before a turn or lane change?",
 "At least 3 seconds", ["At least 1 second", "At least 10 seconds", "Only as you turn"],
 "Signal at least 3 seconds in advance so others can act on it in time, and cancel it afterwards."),
("Why must you cancel your indicator after a turn?",
 "Others may pull out on you", ["It drains the battery", "It dazzles riders behind", "It locks the steering"],
 "A signal still flashing after a turn may make other drivers think you are turning again and pull out in front of you."),
("Turning left from a minor road into a major road, when may you proceed?",
 "Right-side traffic over 6 s away", ["Right-side traffic 2 s away", "Once the road ahead is clear", "Left-side traffic has stopped"],
 "Stop at the stop line, check traffic from the right and go only when it is more than 6 seconds away, after a last check of your left blind spot."),
("Turning right out of a minor road, how far away should traffic from the left be?",
 "About 8 seconds", ["About 2 seconds", "About 4 seconds", "About 20 seconds"],
 "For a right turn the handbook asks for traffic from the right to be more than 6 seconds away and traffic from the left about 8 seconds away."),
("At a left filter lane, you must give way to:",
 "Pedestrians, then the right", ["Only traffic from the left", "Only right-turning traffic", "Nobody; the filter is yours"],
 "Stop behind the white line for pedestrians at the crossing, then give way to approaching vehicles on the right before merging."),
("Turning right at a traffic light, your view is blocked by vehicles turning right from the opposite side. You should:",
 "Wait for the green arrow", ["Edge out past them slowly", "Follow the car in front closely", "Turn quickly between gaps"],
 "If your view is blocked by opposite right-turning vehicles, do not proceed until the green right-turn arrow appears."),
("Making a permitted U-turn where a stop line is marked in the centre of the exit, you should:",
 "Stop behind it until it is safe", ["Ride over it without slowing", "Stop past it, in the opposing lane", "Sound your horn and turn"],
 "Stop behind the stop line, make sure you will not interrupt the flow of traffic, check your blind spot and turn when safe."),
("Road works block your side of a road with a continuous white centre line. You may:",
 "Cross it with care when clear", ["Never cross it at all", "Cross it only at night", "Ride along the footpath"],
 "When road works or parked vehicles block your path, you may cross the centre continuous white line, but only after making sure your intended path is safe and clear."),
("Which riders does the handbook single out as needing to keep left?",
 "Small motorcycles", ["Riders turning right", "Riders overtaking", "Riders on slip roads"],
 "Slow-moving vehicles, which the handbook says includes small capacity motorcycles, goods vehicles and lorries, should keep to the left."),
("In a traffic queue, why leave a gap where a side road joins?",
 "So others can turn in and out", ["So you can filter through it", "So buses can stop there", "So you can overtake later"],
 "Leave a gap at the side road so vehicles from the opposite direction can turn right into it and vehicles from the side road can move out. Do not jump the queue."),
("Pulling over for a fire engine with its siren on, why switch on your indicator?",
 "It shows you have seen it", ["It makes the fire engine stop", "It tells pedestrians to cross", "It is needed only at night"],
 "The handbook says to signal as you pull to the nearest edge, which tells the emergency vehicle's driver you are aware of it and are giving way."),
("Giving way to an emergency vehicle, where must you not stop?",
 "On a bridge or a crest", ["At the left edge of a straight", "In an empty bus bay", "Beside a wide shoulder"],
 "Do not stop on a bridge, curve or hill crest. Signal, carry on until you can pull over safely, and never block a junction."),
("In your mirror, a following car's image is getting bigger. This means it is:",
 "Going faster than you", ["Going slower than you", "Going the same speed", "Stopping behind you"],
 "A growing image means the vehicle is closing in. A steady size means the same speed; a shrinking image means it is slower."),
("Why should you only glance at your mirrors, not stare into them?",
 "Your eyes leave the road", ["The glass may mist up", "The mirror may move", "It dazzles your eyes"],
 "Take quick glances. Looking into the mirror too long takes your attention away from the road ahead."),
("The traffic behind is far back but closing fast as you want to change lanes. The handbook suggests:",
 "Speed up and merge", ["Brake, then change lanes", "Stop in your lane to wait", "Change lanes, then slow"],
 "If the gap is big but the traffic is fast, accelerate to its speed and merge so that you do not force it to brake."),
("Near a junction you find you are in the wrong lane for your direction. You should:",
 "Avoid a sudden lane change", ["Cut across as late as you can", "Stop and wait for a gap", "Reverse back to the right lane"],
 "Lane markings at junctions must be obeyed. Do not change lanes suddenly; get into the correct lane early next time."),
("Approaching a junction on a green light, the handbook says you should:",
 "Ease off, ready to stop", ["Speed up before it changes", "Hold your speed and carry on", "Move into the shared lane"],
 "Do not accelerate towards a signalised junction. Reducing speed lets you slow evenly if the light changes from green to amber."),
("In a traffic hold-up, it is courteous to let vehicles out of a minor road even when:",
 "There is no yellow box", ["Their lights are red", "They have not signalled", "You are on probation"],
 "The handbook says it is courteous to allow vehicles from the minor road to proceed in a hold-up even in the absence of a yellow box."),
("Going straight at a junction, why avoid a lane shared by straight-on and right-turning traffic?",
 "You may block right-turners", ["It is closed to motorcycles", "It is only for buses", "Its red light lasts longer"],
 "If you go straight, avoid the shared lane so you do not hold up right-turning vehicles when the straight-ahead light turns red."),
("Once you are riding round a roundabout, when should you take extra care?",
 "When passing an exit", ["Only as you enter it", "Only when it is empty", "When you reach full speed"],
 "Inside a roundabout, give way to vehicles crossing in front of you and be cautious when passing an exit or about to leave by the next one."),
("Turning left at a traffic light junction, where in your lane should you ride?",
 "On the left side of it", ["On the right side of it", "In the centre of it", "Across the lane line"],
 "Signal at least 3 seconds before the turn, check your left blind spot and keep to the left side of the lane, then slow and change down."),
]
